好，所以我们现在有 99% 和 0%，安迪。
Okay, so we've got 99% and 0%, Andy.

101
00:06:14,990 --> 00:06:21,330
我在我的零前面加个波浪号，因为永远不要说“绝不”，但四舍五入就是 0%。
I put a tilde in front of my zero because never say never, but rounding error 0%.

102
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:30,950
而且我认为这种讨论严重分散了我们对 AI 更实质性、更重要的对话。
And I think this discussion is a massive distraction from the more substantive conversations,
the more important conversations we should be having about AI.

103
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:41,170
我再说一遍，它让我们忽略了 AI 为我们带来的种种好处。
And I'll say it again, it distracts us from the good things that AI is doing, will be doing for us.

104
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:50,250
有时我从 AI 社区的一部分人那里得到的印象是，
这是一种被释放到世界上的巨大邪恶或可怕的事情。
I get this impression sometimes from parts of the AI community that this
is a massive evil or a terrible thing that has been unleashed on the world.

105
00:06:50,390 --> 00:07:04,910
除非我们听取那些花大量时间思考这个问题的人的建议，否则从很多讨论中我得到的印象是，
底层的观点是：如果 AI 从未被发明，我们的处境会更好。
Unless we listen to the advice of some people who have spent a lot of time thinking about this,
I get the impression from a lot of the discussion that the underlying view is we would be better off had AI never been invented.

106
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,450
我强烈反对这种观点。
I vehemently reject that view.

107
00:07:08,450 --> 00:07:14,730
我认为我们有一段很长的历史，一直在发明具有强大功能的技术，
而这些技术也伴随着风险和危害。
I think we have a long history of inventing very powerful technologies that bring risks and harms along with them.

108
00:07:14,810 --> 00:07:26,070
而且我们人类在处理这些情况方面做得很好，虽然不是完美且立即的，但我们通过摸索前进，
并最终因为拥有新技术而处境变得更好。
And we humans have done a really good job at, you know, not perfectly and not immediately,
