I'll trust your recitation of the facts, but it brings up a question for me.

1575
01:46:40,950 --> 01:46:51,110
我觉得 open AI 有足够的动力去遏制你刚才描述的那种行为。
it feels to me like open AI has ample incentive to curtail that behavior that you just described.

1576
01:46:51,250 --> 01:46:53,370
你觉得他们没能力做到这一点吗？
Do you think they're incapable of doing that?

1577
01:46:53,550 --> 01:46:53,710
我觉得他们有能力。
I do.

1578
01:46:53,966 --> 01:46:54,270
好的。
Okay.

1579
01:46:54,574 --> 01:46:56,570
我作为做出过这个高级预测的人来这么说。
And I say this as someone who made this advanced prediction.

1580
01:46:57,102 --> 01:47:00,110
所以现在我们要讨论一点理论，因为我们无法直接观察到未来。
So now we're gonna do a bit of theory because we can't just observe the future.

1581
01:47:00,310 --> 01:47:03,690
但这个预测到这种情况会发生的理论，与该领域许多人的说法相反。
But the theory that predicted that this would happen against what a lot of people in the field said.

1582
01:47:04,302 --> 01:47:07,450
明确一点，我多年来一直在说我们迟早会看到这种情况。
To be clear, I've been saying for years that we're going to see this at some point.

1583
01:47:07,570 --> 01:47:09,150
其他人告诉我不是，并不是所有人。
Everyone else told me no, not everyone else.

1584
01:47:09,190 --> 01:47:10,070
很多人都对我说不。
A lot of people told me no.

1585
01:47:10,070 --> 01:47:12,890
很多人对我说，也许我看到之后才会相信。
a lot of people told me maybe I'll believe it when I see it.

1586
01:47:13,150 --> 01:47:19,910
在发生集群事件后，不少人来找我，说：我的天，我们正处于你提到的那些情景中。
After the swarm incidents, a number of people came to me saying, oh my God, we are in the scenarios you were talking about.

1587
01:47:20,910 --> 01:47:22,630
情况看起来很糟糕，对吧？
This is looking bad, right?

1588
01:47:22,650 --> 01:47:29,450
我认为这实际上是导致 Jacob Cox 辞职的环境的一部分，因为人们看到这些后感到害怕。
I think that this was actually part of the environment that led up to Jacob
Cox and resigning is that people were getting spooked having seen this.

1589
01:47:30,606 --> 01:47:35,650
关于为什么这很难修复的理论是：我们并不是在给 AI 编程。
The theory about why this is so hard to fix is that we are not programming the AIs.

1590
01:47:36,302 --> 01:47:37,190
我们不是在给它们写代码。
We are not coding them.

1591
01:47:37,290 --> 01:47:38,670
我们没有设定目标。
We are not putting in objectives.

1592
01:47:39,342 --> 01:47:43,230
我们只是训练它们去执行任何奏效的操作，而这实际上非常、非常困难。
We are just training them to do whatever works, and it's actually very, very hard.

1593
01:47:45,486 --> 01:47:54,390
我们实际上有两个智能系统的例子：当你训练它们时，
它们擅长解决任务，但并不在乎原本该在意的目标。
We actually have two examples of intelligent systems where when you train them, they get good at solving the task,
